Chapter: SystemDb
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 System database stored on the USB boot stick. Uses the DiskFacts
 format (dual-sector superblock, append-only fact log) to persist
 identity, boot configuration, trust vouches, and drive registry.

 The system DB lives at a known path on the stick's FAT32 ESP:
 CODEX/SYSDB.BIN. On first boot, the file does not exist and the
 system enters the first-boot ceremony.

 To sysdb-is-fresh gives Boolean, True when no identity exists.
 To sysdb-load-identity gives Maybe IdentityRecord after passphrase unlock.
 To sysdb-save-identity encrypts and stores a new identity.
 To sysdb-load-boot-config gives Maybe SysBootConfig.
 To sysdb-save-boot-config persists boot configuration.

 We say:

Section: Types

  IdentityRecord = record {
    id-version : Integer,
    id-salt : List Integer,
    id-iv : List Integer,
    id-encrypted-key : List Integer,
    id-public-key : List Integer,
    id-created-ticks : Integer
  }

  SysBootConfig = record {
    sbc-boot-mode : Integer,
    sbc-boot-drive-serial : Text,
    sbc-boot-partition : Integer
  }

  DriveRecord = record {
    dr-serial : Text,
    dr-label : Text,
    dr-size-mb : Integer,
    dr-last-seen : Integer
  }

Section: Constants

  sysdb-kind-identity : Integer = 10
  sysdb-kind-boot-config : Integer = 11
  sysdb-kind-trust-vouch : Integer = 12
  sysdb-kind-drive-registry : Integer = 13
  sysdb-kind-installed-os : Integer = 14

  sysdb-boot-mode-console : Integer = 0
  sysdb-boot-mode-ui : Integer = 1
  sysdb-boot-mode-serial : Integer = 2


